WEBVTT

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:02.980
Your duo name will be "MEZZO"."

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.210
Is it really impossible?

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:06.150
To let them debut together...

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:10.030
If doing their best was enough, 
everyone could be a star tomorrow.

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:12.360
I hope we can perform
 as a team of seven soon...

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.990
Let's think of ways we can do that.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:20.790
I wish I could embrace you right now

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:26.000
And run away with you

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.250
But I can't so my small love

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:35.850
Will never reach you

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:50.650
Your voices really do mesh
 together perfectly.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.420
You're the perfect combo.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:53.690
Sure...

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:57.380
Why don't you two look happy?

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:02.680
By the way, you've been sticking 
with us for a while now.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:04.370
Are the other five doing okay?

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:06.060
That's right.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:08.750
You two have more work right now.

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:12.820
I wish you could each have
 your own managers.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:14.030
You can't do that.

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:16.760
You won't be able to 
promote IDOLiSH7 that way.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.330
That's actually something 
I'd like to discuss.

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:24.520
I hate to ask, but could you handle 
your work on your own a little more?

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:29.940
Sure. MEZZO"'s good, but I want 
people to call us IDOLiSH7 soon.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:31.270
You're right.

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:34.900
We'll do whatever the two of us can do.

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:38.660
I'm sorry. If only I were better at this...

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:41.040
We'll be fine.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.380
So-chan pays attention to detail,

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:44.560
and does everything five minutes early.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:46.710
It's all so the seven of us 
can work together soon.

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:49.670
Yeah, so we can work as seven.

00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:53.500
Thank you.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:57.010
I'll do my best to promote IDOLiSH7!

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:06.180
Gazing at the distant sky...

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:09.730
Someday we'll make it past there

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:15.860
Build a rainbow Next Harmony!

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:22.160
We don't know what's right

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:25.370
So we Try and Jump!

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:28.540
Slamming face first into 
challenges and laughing

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:32.170
For us It's Only Way!

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:35.340
Make it shake (For Your Sky)

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:38.920
Make it reach (For Your Heart)

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:41.340
We'll change any and all kinds of pain

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:42.510
Do Live! (Yeah!)

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:43.350
Live! (Yeah!)

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:46.760
In the light!

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.850
(One, Two, Three, Four, Five, Six, Seven Go!)

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:54.020
Yes Glory Days! Together 
we'll run through them

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:56.820
If your voice (Fuu!) reverberates (Dream!)

00:02:56.820 --> 00:03:00.320
Then your wishes will become 
destiny (Singing New World!)

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:06.850
Give rise now to Age of Stage!

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:13.790
The future surely lies on the other side

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:16.710
Yes... It will keep on evolving

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:20.090
Our WiSH VOYAGE

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:26.350
Build a rainbow Next Harmony!

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:34.980
#10 Expanding World

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:36.810
A web show?

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:39.990
Yes. Until now we've focused on concerts,

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:44.240
but I'm thinking about emphasizing 
internet projects going forward.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.410
You're right.

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:48.660
Our concerts felt off 
without the other two.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.820
When there's seven of us on 
the poster but only five performing,

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:53.460
it does seem incomplete.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.570
It's not a bad idea.

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:59.340
The videos of us that have been
 uploaded have gotten a lot of views.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:01.550
Why? Why is that?

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:03.840
I wish I could say it's 
because of our talent,

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:07.430
but it's probably because 
of the unexpected incidents.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:11.980
Yeah. We performed a concert in 
a storm and had a power outage.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:15.900
Scary for us, but I guess it's entertaining
 when it's not happening to you.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:20.250
We do have one video with a lot of 
views unrelated to those incidents.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:21.150
Which?

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:23.860
Our disastrous first concert.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:25.780
Oh, that.

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:29.490
The agency actually didn't 
want that video uploaded...

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.810
Look at all those views.

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:32.950
I wonder why.

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:36.080
Because we look like we're having fun.

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:40.130
We're light on our feet. We're all smiling.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.550
We look like we're having fun...

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:45.550
Your voice was at its highest 
quality during this concert.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:49.680
If only you could perform 
like this every time.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.660
I wish I could, too!

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:53.100
I'll try...

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:55.460
Okay, okay. Calm down.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:58.400
In any case, we're doing a web show, right?

00:04:58.610 --> 00:04:59.900
Ah, yes.

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:04.530
Okay. What's the title of our show?

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:08.280
Ahem. It's...

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:13.620
"IDOLiSH Night With You!"

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:12.060
Web Show Plan

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:12.060
<b>ID♥LiSH Night With You!</b>

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:16.700
Isn't that embarrassing?

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:19.050
I feel like I'm too old for that.

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:19.710
Right?

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:20.790
Huh?

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:22.050
Huh?

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:26.260
It's huge.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:28.430
I won it at an arcade.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:31.810
Should we do a King Pudding 
and Cocona collab?

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:33.290
We can't use either of them!

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:34.770
We'll get in trouble.

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:36.770
Copyright issues are scary.

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:38.940
But it's cute.

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:41.430
Here, Tamaki-kun.

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:43.050
If you do this...

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:44.360
It kinda looks like King Pudding.

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:46.610
That looks nothing like him.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:48.740
So-chan, you don't get it.

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:52.070
Tamaki-san, Sogo-san. We should get going.

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:53.370
Oh, work.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:56.020
Sorry. We'll be back soon.

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:57.500
We'll be fine here.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.000
Good luck at work!

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:00.930
Bye, everyone.

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:02.290
Bye!

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:06.130
Sorry for having you guys build the set.

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:09.260
It's fine. We said we wanted to do it.

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:15.640
Some of our fans were happy when MEZZO" 
debuted, but some of them were shocked.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:17.290
You're right.

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:21.400
The complaint calls kept pouring in that day.

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:25.090
Failing to meet their expectations 
was really disappointing.

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:28.360
But more than that, I was happy.

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:30.820
They felt the same way we did, at least.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:34.660
It made me feel like I have to see things 
through and gave me tons of courage.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:39.040
Yeah. They're all waiting for our debut.

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:43.950
Okay, let's have fun.

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:46.380
Let's try things other 
than singing and dancing.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:48.670
That sounds fun.

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:51.920
Idols should expand their range of activity.

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:53.600
Like variety shows and dramas.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:54.890
Dramas, huh?

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:57.980
Acting might be too hard for us.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:00.430
I'd recommend Nikaido-san.

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:01.440
Why?

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:03.580
You're very expressive.

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:04.360
You're right.

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:07.210
Yamato-san, maybe you'd like to audition for—

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:08.180
Sorry, but I'm not interested.

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:09.030
Huh?

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:10.950
Ask someone else.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:12.670
I see.

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:15.450
Get back to work.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:18.340
We can't start our show until we finish this.

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:19.660
Okay.

00:07:20.110 --> 00:07:24.030
If we're going to be in dramas, 
I want to play the bad guy.

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:27.060
I'll be the spy of a mysterious organization.

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:29.670
I think I'd prefer being a hero.

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:31.550
Like a righteous police officer.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:35.390
Nanase-san, wouldn't you make 
a better kidnapped heroine?

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:37.810
You're totally trying to 
pick a fight, aren't you?!

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:39.810
Gonna ignore me now, huh?!

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:40.550
Hey, Iori!

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:42.560
You wanna fight?! Huh?!

00:07:45.050 --> 00:07:46.570
We're starting.

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:49.810
Five seconds, four, three...

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:54.260
Good evening.

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:55.750
This is "IDOLiSH Night With You."

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:56.950
I'm Nanase Riku!

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:58.650
I'm Izumi Iori.

00:07:56.950 --> 00:08:01.580
<b>ID♥LiSH Night With You</b>

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:00.400
I'm Nikaido Yamato.

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:01.580
I'm Izumi Mitsuki.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:05.610
I'm Nagi Valhart von North...

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:07.160
Sorry, stop the camera.

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:08.210
What?

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:10.240
Mitsukiii...

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:11.510
That hurts!

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:14.340
Don't make your name sound all fancy.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:15.610
Say your real name!

00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:16.660
My real name?

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:19.350
But that <i>is</i> my name.

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:19.350
<b>We're live!</b>

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:21.470
What? We're live?!

00:08:21.470 --> 00:08:22.890
We're doing this live?!

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:25.020
That's what you meant?!

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:28.310
You should've told us beforehand!

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:31.460
Calm down. Don't drop your board.

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:33.700
<b>I'm sorry I forgot to tell you!</b>

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:38.780
Um, anyway, our first segment is 
"I'm sorry I forgot to tell you."

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:40.200
Let's check it out!

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.910
No, no. That's not the name of the segment.

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:45.030
Turn the page! Turn the page!

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:45.040
Sorry, sorry.

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:51.000
Good evening!

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:54.380
This is "IDOLiSH Night With You," 
and I'm Izumi Mitsuki.

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:57.800
Tonight, we're setting up 
dominoes together.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:01.560
Try to guess the image
 we're making, everybody!

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:03.780
Isn't this kinda boring?

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:04.980
Shut up!

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:06.940
Just be energetic and line them up!

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:09.370
I just want to knock them down.

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:10.940
Everyone does!

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:13.680
Okay, let's play rock paper scissors.

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:15.950
The loser will line them up.

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:18.700
I'm not good at rock paper scissors.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:22.580
I bet you always throw paper.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:24.400
Hey, you might be right.

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:25.410
How did you know?

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:29.560
You subconsciously choose the hand that 
will beat whatever you were just shown.

00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:30.910
If you lack ingenuity.

00:09:30.910 --> 00:09:33.550
God, you're annoying...

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:35.620
I'll line them up, then.

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:37.220
You guys can do something else.

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:39.190
Really? Thanks.

00:09:39.190 --> 00:09:41.420
You're so nice, Sogo-san.

00:09:41.420 --> 00:09:45.620
Come to think of it, I watched the 
music show MEZZO" was on the other day.

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:47.760
Really? Thanks.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:53.690
That reminds me, I should return 
the concert DVD you let me borrow.

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:57.750
I'll lend you one of my 
<i>Magical Cocona</i> DVDs, too.

00:09:57.750 --> 00:09:59.460
Huh? So you're forcing me to take it?

00:09:59.460 --> 00:10:01.120
I'm just trying to thank you.

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:03.540
I've already watched it twice.

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:05.660
Listen to this, he—

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:07.870
How long are we going to keep doing this?

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:09.660
I'm hungry.

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:11.590
You just had some pudding.

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:13.100
You sure do eat a lot.

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:16.130
Guys, do you even realize 
we're in the middle of—

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:20.220
There.

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:22.390
S-Sorry.

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:24.180
Way to go, Leader.

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:25.940
Hey, Leader!

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:27.930
You don't need to flatter me.

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:36.310
Good evening.

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:39.450
This is "IDOLiSH Night With You,"
 and I'm Nikaido Yamato.

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:42.850
Tonight, we'll be reading the letters 
we asked you to submit last time.

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:44.580
Wow. It's like a real show.

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:45.950
Thanks for all the letters.

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:45.950
He's doing a great job.

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:48.500
That's not very many comments.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:50.120
Don't say that.

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:52.660
Here's our first letter:

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:57.130
"Why did only Sogo-kun and Tamaki-kun debut?"

00:10:57.130 --> 00:11:00.350
That came as a shock to me, too.

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:02.340
It all started when they were recruited by—

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:04.920
Are you insane?

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:07.310
You should know what can and can't be said.

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:10.580
Should we answer their question with a lie?

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:12.850
Please don't say the word "lie!"

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:12.850
<b>Lie</b>

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:12.850
<b>Deceit</b>

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:12.850
<b>Exaggeration</b>

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:12.850
<b>Confusion</b>

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:15.510
We can't tell you the truth.

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:17.080
But it's not what we wanted.

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:17.640
What?

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:18.190
Okay, next.

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:21.030
Yamato-san, it's not what you wanted either?

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:24.370
You guys worked really hard.

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:26.080
I wanted to do something for you.

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:29.970
Please stop spreading rumors.

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:32.460
<b>ID♥LiSH Night With You!</b>

00:11:29.970 --> 00:11:32.460
"IDOLiSH Night With You!"

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:34.460
<b>Act out a police drama!</b>

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:35.730
Nii-san, it's an emergency!

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:36.920
What's wrong, Iceman?

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:38.830
Our new officer Nanase-san

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:42.020
was kidnapped by an international 
terrorist organization, Codename 256.

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:43.850
Also, please don't call me Iceman.

00:11:43.850 --> 00:11:46.550
Seriously?! But he's a cop!

00:11:46.550 --> 00:11:47.780
We need to rescue him.

00:11:47.780 --> 00:11:48.810
Let's go, Iceman!

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:50.480
Please stop calling me Iceman.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:52.330
Am I on yet?

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:54.980
Yamato, you're really not 
going to be in the show?

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:59.610
An evil leader doesn't often 
make appearances, after all.

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:02.110
<b>ID♥LiSH Night With You!</b>

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:02.110
"IDOLiSH Night With You!"

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:02.970
Good evening!

00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:05.580
Tonight, we're cooking!

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:08.180
Since Tamaki works so hard all the time,

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:12.120
we're going to surprise 
him with a giant pudding.

00:12:12.110 --> 00:12:13.670
What are you guys doing?

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:16.170
Yotsuba-san, aren't you working?

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:17.900
I finished early.

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:18.960
What are you guys doing?

00:12:24.350 --> 00:12:26.470
That's good.

00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:30.760
We're trying again!

00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:34.120
Today we made dishes Sogo would like.

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:35.750
Thanks for making this for me.

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:36.940
I'm really happy.

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:39.450
Nice reaction.

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:41.110
Did we succeed this time?

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:43.680
I imagine that depends on our cooking.

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:45.840
Well, we followed the recipe.

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:47.390
There shouldn't be any—

00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:52.350
It's really good!

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:53.960
You're all such good cooks.

00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:56.850
Are you for real, So?

00:12:56.850 --> 00:12:57.610
Huh?

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:01.210
Did you watch "IDOLiSH Night With You?"

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:02.810
Isn't it funny?

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:03.820
I know what you mean.

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:05.900
I like how unpolished it is.

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:08.270
MEZZO"'s Sogo and Tamaki talk a lot, too.

00:13:08.270 --> 00:13:10.720
I know. I thought they were cooler types.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:13.730
The older Izumi's retorts are so funny.

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:16.770
Isn't it cute how the younger Izumi 
always freaks out even though

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:17.900
he acts so composed?

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:21.130
But they're so handsome when they're singing.

00:13:21.130 --> 00:13:22.130
It's seriously insane.

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:23.570
That's exactly it!

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:26.070
Huh, this looks fun.

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:27.070
Doesn't it?

00:13:27.070 --> 00:13:29.910
I saw their concert video, 
and it was pretty good.

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:31.990
It was totally different 
from the <i>Music Festa</i>.

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:35.120
I wonder why only MEZZO" debuted.

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:38.890
I'd like to see all seven 
of them perform together.

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:44.880
IDOLiSH Night is on tonight!!

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:44.880
I know! I'm watching it
in the living room!

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:44.880
Sogo-san was so cool. 
I can't handle it...

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:44.880
I hope they can 
debut together soon.

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:50.380
Japan Media Service?

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:53.460
A d-drama director?!

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:54.640
Is something wrong?!

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:57.580
Yamato-san got an offer for an acting job!

00:14:01.370 --> 00:14:03.080
I'm not really interested.

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:04.320
What?

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:05.930
Why not do it?

00:14:05.930 --> 00:14:07.700
Please don't waste this opportunity.

00:14:08.020 --> 00:14:09.220
He's right!

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:10.750
It's a two hour drama.

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:12.610
And it's during prime time.

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:13.450
Really?

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:17.140
It's a school detective show, and you'd 
be playing the teacher who gets killed.

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:18.660
Wow, that's perfect for you!

00:14:18.660 --> 00:14:20.660
How is that perfect?

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:23.630
Uh, well... you know, just overall.

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:27.930
Yamato, it says you're popular among women.

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:31.240
My instincts are telling me that 
the person who murdered you

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:33.660
is afflicted with jealousy.

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:35.310
Does that ring any bells?!

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:37.510
Nobody's actually murdered me!

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:41.790
Who's the director that contacted you?

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:43.620
Kinoshita Masami.

00:14:44.810 --> 00:14:46.770
That old man, huh?

00:14:46.770 --> 00:14:49.860
Sorry, but I'm not interested in acting.

00:14:50.100 --> 00:14:51.260
Let them know I said no.

00:14:52.590 --> 00:14:54.120
Yamato-san...

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:56.350
Okay, that's all for today.

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:57.780
Good work, guys.

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:03.070
Maybe he knows the director.

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:05.500
What? You mean he was an actor?

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:09.180
His resume didn't mention 
anything about that.

00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:10.580
Too bad.

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:12.910
It could've been a great opportunity.

00:15:19.220 --> 00:15:20.520
Yamato-san.

00:15:21.590 --> 00:15:23.140
What is it, Manager?

00:15:23.140 --> 00:15:24.940
Joining me for a drink?

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:26.390
No, um...

00:15:26.870 --> 00:15:28.690
Why are you so desperate to avoid them?

00:15:29.090 --> 00:15:30.350
Huh?

00:15:30.350 --> 00:15:31.700
Dramas.

00:15:32.150 --> 00:15:35.310
If you don't mind, could you tell me why?

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:38.450
I'm not good at memorizing lines.

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:42.620
But you learn lyrics and 
choreography faster than—

00:15:41.650 --> 00:15:43.710
No, I don't.

00:15:44.260 --> 00:15:49.280
If I hadn't become an idol, I would've 
found a job as a salaryman.

00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:51.720
I'm your average ordinary 22-year-old.

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:54.470
Then why did you become an idol?

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:58.140
Revenge.

00:15:58.140 --> 00:15:59.180
Huh?

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:00.980
I'm joking!

00:16:01.580 --> 00:16:02.790
That's cold!

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:03.940
Huh? Um...

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:09.670
Don't you prefer a man 
who's a little mysterious?

00:16:12.940 --> 00:16:14.240
Still joking.

00:16:15.110 --> 00:16:16.240
Yamato-san!

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:17.890
Now, now.

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:22.410
I'll do anything besides acting 
if it'll help promote them.

00:16:22.970 --> 00:16:24.500
I'll do my best.

00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:35.340
Damn!

00:16:37.190 --> 00:16:39.030
I was offbeat again.

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:44.810
Mitsu, still practicing?

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:48.850
Sometimes my dancing's out 
of sync with everyone else.

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:53.740
I'm doing the same thing, so 
where am I getting offbeat?

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:55.250
Of course you are.

00:16:55.250 --> 00:16:58.170
You're small, so your strides are shorter.

00:16:58.170 --> 00:17:00.240
You get offbeat when you change positions.

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:02.660
Oh, that's it!

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:04.410
Okay, one more time!

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:09.180
You're always working so hard.

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:11.160
Of course I am.

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:13.380
It wouldn't be any fun otherwise!

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:18.050
If you only try moderately 
hard and moderately succeed,

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:20.560
then you'll only be moderately happy.

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:25.270
So I'd rather try as hard as I can,
 succeed as best as I can,

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:26.980
and be as happy as I can.

00:17:28.130 --> 00:17:30.020
Don't you think that feels better?

00:17:31.380 --> 00:17:33.250
You only live once,

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:37.230
and I'm the only one who can make my life fun!

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:38.990
Mitsu...

00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:43.150
Yamato-san, you should try it, too.

00:17:43.730 --> 00:17:45.870
I don't know what you've been through,

00:17:46.180 --> 00:17:52.880
but I want to see you cry real tears 
of frustration and real tears of joy.

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:56.380
Show me, Leader.

00:17:57.730 --> 00:18:00.470
Mitsuki, let us join you!

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:02.720
What are you guys doing here?

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:05.430
We could see you from inside.

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:07.010
Let's dance!

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:08.770
It's party time!

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:10.560
This is practice.

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:12.390
Yeah! Let's party!

00:18:12.390 --> 00:18:13.730
Join us, Leader!

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:19.870
Being the leader's hard.

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:22.200
Here, Yamato-san.

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:22.190
The 16-Year-Old
 Classroom 2

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:23.760
Thanks.

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:25.040
You seem happy.

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:26.230
Of course.

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:29.700
This is IDOLiSH7's first drama.

00:18:29.700 --> 00:18:31.960
I'm glad you're breaking new ground.

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:34.980
Everyone believes in you, Yamato-san.

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:37.550
Your flattery won't get you anywhere.

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:39.680
You'll make tons of money.

00:18:39.990 --> 00:18:43.210
We'll be able to feed
 the others fancy lunches.

00:18:43.210 --> 00:18:47.890
Guess I'll try doing my best.

00:18:48.380 --> 00:18:51.530
Why did you suddenly
change your mind, though?

00:18:51.530 --> 00:18:52.310
Yeah.

00:18:53.580 --> 00:18:56.070
The 16-Year-Old
 Classroom 2

00:18:54.090 --> 00:18:56.070
It's a secret.

00:18:57.020 --> 00:19:00.740
Homeroom teacher Kumaga, played by 
Nikaido Yamato-san, is entering the set.

00:19:03.420 --> 00:19:04.900
Thanks for having me!

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:10.580
Yamato-san's drama is on soon.

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:12.490
I'm nervous.

00:19:12.490 --> 00:19:14.580
Nanase-san, this has nothing to do with you.

00:19:14.580 --> 00:19:16.420
Sure it does! We're in the same group.

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:20.510
Why aren't we watching in my theater room?

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:21.930
Because that's <i>my</i> room!

00:19:21.930 --> 00:19:24.670
You just set up your speakers 
and crap in there!

00:19:24.670 --> 00:19:28.770
Could you do something about the mountain 
of clothes you left in my room?

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:31.480
Ah, and all the cups in my room.

00:19:31.830 --> 00:19:33.350
<b>The 16-Year-Old Classroom 2</b>

00:19:31.830 --> 00:19:33.350
G-Guys, the show...

00:19:36.030 --> 00:19:37.360
It's starting!

00:19:37.850 --> 00:19:39.950
<i>Let's get homeroom started.</i>

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:41.400
<i>Hurry and take your seats.</i>

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:45.420
He's so cool. He's like a teacher.

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:48.650
Yama-san should watch it with us.

00:19:48.650 --> 00:19:50.290
He's probably embarrassed.

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:53.710
<i>As you all know, lately there's been</i>

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:58.620
<i>an increase in the number of suspicious 
figures spotted around school.</i>

00:19:54.590 --> 00:19:57.210
Isn't he... a super good actor?

00:19:57.210 --> 00:20:02.380
Maybe I'm biased, but won't 
he steal the spotlight at this rate?

00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:06.510
It's like he's not Yama-san.

00:20:06.510 --> 00:20:08.420
<i>Wait! Don't move!</i>

00:20:08.420 --> 00:20:10.480
<i>Please don't go!</i>

00:20:12.210 --> 00:20:15.400
<i>I couldn't understand how they felt!</i>

00:20:16.130 --> 00:20:18.860
<i>I've failed as a teacher...</i>

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:25.050
This expression...

00:20:25.050 --> 00:20:27.430
Nagi-san, is something wrong?

00:20:27.430 --> 00:20:29.490
It's nothing.

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:35.000
I can't believe Yamato-san 
was hiding this talent.

00:20:31.820 --> 00:20:35.000
<i>Why don't you believe in yourself?!
Why are you running from yourself?!</i>

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:38.500
<i>It may still be a lie.</i>

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:41.170
<i>He likely had some other motivation though.</i>

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:45.760
<i>But those feelings... They're not a lie.</i>

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:45.760
The 16-Year-Old 
Classroom 2

00:20:46.810 --> 00:20:47.660
Did you know?

00:20:47.660 --> 00:20:49.950
Nikaido Yamato's an idol.

00:20:49.950 --> 00:20:51.600
What? He's not an actor?

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:53.730
He's in IDOLiSH7.

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:55.730
He's in the same group as MEZZO".

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:59.450
Oh, wow. I wanna see them perform now.

00:21:01.470 --> 00:21:02.220
Wanna go?

00:21:02.220 --> 00:21:03.950
Yes!

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:06.410
<b>ID♥LiSH Night With You!</b>

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:06.410
IDOLiSH Night With You!

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:08.210
This is "IDOLiSH Night With You!"

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:09.370
I'm Nanase Riku.

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:13.250
Did you watch our two hour
 drama the other day?

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:16.020
As you know, Nikaido-san was in it.

00:21:16.020 --> 00:21:17.970
You were awesome.

00:21:17.970 --> 00:21:18.880
Even if you got murdered.

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:20.630
You were just like a real teacher.

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:21.750
Even if you got murdered.

00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:26.880
The murderer was motivated 
by their jealousy for Yamato.

00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:29.710
Sometimes love kills Yamato!

00:21:29.710 --> 00:21:30.430
Rest in peace.

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:33.390
I told you, I'm not dead.

00:21:33.930 --> 00:21:36.950
Wow, the comments are coming in really fast!

00:21:36.950 --> 00:21:39.440
Whoa, there's way more people watching!

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:42.630
Okay, let's make this even more fun!

00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:45.900
Yamato is announcing his next drama.

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:48.510
Rokuya-san, we're announcing that at the end.

00:21:48.510 --> 00:21:49.640
Follow the script.

00:21:49.640 --> 00:21:51.600
Yeah, I'm in another drama.

00:21:51.600 --> 00:21:54.160
But we have a concert before that.

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:55.580
I hope you'll watch that, too.

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:59.820
Yeah, and we have a group 
interview in next week's issue

00:21:59.820 --> 00:22:02.180
of monthly magazine <i>Live Collection</i>.

00:21:59.900 --> 00:22:02.540
But that's...

00:22:02.180 --> 00:22:03.170
It's brief, though.

00:22:02.540 --> 00:22:03.170
Nii-san!

00:22:03.170 --> 00:22:05.900
We're starting to get more work as a group.

00:22:05.900 --> 00:22:08.650
Yeah, thanks to all your support.

00:22:08.650 --> 00:22:10.070
Thank you.

00:22:10.070 --> 00:22:14.000
Now with gratitude in 
our hearts, let us sing.

00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:14.850
Listen to this.

00:22:14.850 --> 00:22:16.730
I said, follow the script!

00:22:17.510 --> 00:22:18.980
I can't keep up with the comments!

00:22:34.410 --> 00:22:37.950
Start running (beyond)

00:22:37.950 --> 00:22:44.810
Your imagination... Alive

00:22:53.050 --> 00:22:58.610
If you desire something from 
the bottom of your heart

00:22:58.610 --> 00:23:03.270
Risk your life and dive in

00:23:03.270 --> 00:23:08.360
The resolve to discard what's truly important

00:23:08.360 --> 00:23:13.490
Is the boat that will take you to new sights

00:23:13.490 --> 00:23:16.040
(Hey man!) Take the strings of your heart

00:23:16.390 --> 00:23:18.580
(Hey man!) And stretch them

00:23:18.580 --> 00:23:21.460
(Say dream!) To the limit

00:23:21.460 --> 00:23:26.380
At the other end you're sure 
to find the Gate to paradise

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:32.450
You'll be the first witness

00:23:32.450 --> 00:23:37.240
Our pounding pulses are Heavenly

00:23:37.240 --> 00:23:42.530
Admit that you can't deny it

00:23:42.530 --> 00:23:46.960
We start... What do your fingertips

00:23:46.960 --> 00:23:51.260
Seek now?
